WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:02.060
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.960
On the TV show Survivor,

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.660
contestants faced off in a winner take all competition

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.900
to try and win one million dollars.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.260
Most of the competitions were physical,

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:17.580
like hiking many miles or diving underwater,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.940
but one of the challenges was mathematical.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.460
It involved 21 flags.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:31.840
The contestants were divided into two teams that would take turns removing flags.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.020
Each team has to remove 1, 2 or 3 flags on a turn.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.480
The team that removed the final flag wins the game.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.860
Mathematically one team can always win this game.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:58.820
The puzzle for you is which team is it and what is that team's winning strategy.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:05.080
Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for the solution.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.320
So what's the winning strategy when there are 21 flags?

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.660
It's not so easy to figure out,

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:20.700
instead we consider the game by thinking ahead and reasoning backward.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:27.740
We try and imagine what would happen if we'd start a turn with a specific number of flags,

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:31.540
and we would decide whether we can win or lose the game on that turn.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.680
So let's say there's just one flag.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:42.020
If you start out with one flag, you can obviously pick up that flag and you will win the game for sure.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:49.100
This  goes for if there are 2 flags you are gonna win the game, and if there are 3 flags you are gonna win the game.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:55.720
With this number of flags you can just pick them all up and you're going to be the one that removes the last flag.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.960
But what happens if there are 4 flags?

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.060
Well you can pick up 1, 2 or 3 flags on your turn.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:12.040
If you pick up 1 flag you leave 3 flags for the other team and the other team is gonna pick up all 3 flags,

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.420
if you pick up 2 flags you'll leave 2 flags for the other team,

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:20.000
but they again can pick up all of those flags.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:27.640
If you try and pick up 3 flags you still leave 1 flag for the other team and they can pick it up and win the game.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:36.760
What this means is if there are 4 flags in front of you no matter what you do you are going to lose this game.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:42.000
You are going to leave a number of flags that your opponent can pick up on the next turn.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.100
What would happen if there are 5 flags?

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:52.600
In this case you could pick up 1 flag and leave 4 flags for your opponent,

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.420
now your opponent is necessarily going to lose,

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:58.180
which means you are necessarily going to win.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:03.040
Similarly if there are 6 or 7 flags.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.120
You could pick those up and leave 4 flags for your opponent,

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.840
this would mean that your opponent is going to lose.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:15.020
So this means 6 or 7 flags is also a winning number of flags.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.300
What would happen if there are 8 flags?

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:30.340
On this case if you try and pick up 1, 2 or 3 flags, no matter what you do you're going to leave a winning number of flags for your opponent.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:38.060
This means if there are 8 flags you are necessarily going to lose the game if your opponent plays correctly.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:42.280
We can now see a pattern in what we've developed,

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:50.620
if the number of flags is a multiple of 4 you are going to lose the game if your opponent plays perfectly.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:57.820
So we can continue this list and we can have the number of flags for when you're going to lose the game and

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.660
the number of flags for when you're going to win the game.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:07.480
You can notice that 21 is in the numbers of flags for which you can win the game.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.100
So if the game starts out with 21 flags,

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:15.360
that means the first team that picks up flags can win this game for sure.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:21.000
By always picking up flags and leaving a multiple of 4 for the other team.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:25.860
So the first team that picks up should win this game.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.300
But let's consider what actually happened on TV.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:34.180
We'll compare the optimal move to what the 2 teams could have picked up.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:41.940
The first move the first team should have picked up 1 flag leaving 20 flags for the other team.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:48.180
Instead they picked up 2 flags leaving 19 flags for team B.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.940
So if team B picked understood the winning strategy,

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:57.680
they could now pick up 3 flags which would leave 16 flags for team A.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.620
Instead team B also picked up 2 flags and left 17 flags.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:07.280
This gives team A an opportunity to redeem itself,

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:11.340
they can now pick up 1 flag and be in a winning position.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:16.240
What they did instead is they picked up 2 flags leaving 15.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:20.240
So now team B if they picked up

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:25.240
3 flags they're gonna be able to leave 12 for team A,

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:26.680
and they're gonna be able to win the game.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.260
What did team B do at this point?

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:35.180
They made another mistake! They picked up 1 flag, leaving 14 flags for team A!

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:41.180
Team A could pick up 2 flags and be again in a winning position,

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:46.740
but they made another mistake! They only picked up 1 flag here and they left 13 flags.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:51.700
Team B finally makes a winning move here!

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.580
they pick up 1 flag and they leave 12 flags.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:06:00.120
So team B is in position to win this game as long as they play correctly the rest of the way.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:04.980
So team A at this point has no choice, they pick up some number of flags,

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.500
if team B plays properly,

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.160
team B is gonna win the game.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:15.140
So when there're 11 flags left team B should pick up 3 flags,

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:17.480
to leave 8 flags for team A.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.920
But team B messes up again!

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:25.820
Here they only pick up 2 flags which leaves 9 flags for team A.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:31.460
So team A could redeem itself by picking up 1 flag and leaving 8.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:33.580
Instead,

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:39.260
they make a big mistake here and pick up 3 flags which leaves 6 flags for team B.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:46.000
Now with 6 flags remaining, team B is able to reason out the winning strategy.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:51.160
So they do correctly pick up 2 flags here and leave 4 flags for team A.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:56.780
This was actually shown on the TV show that they are discussing that they should leave 4 flags for the other team.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.280
At this point team A realizes

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:00.860
that they can not win the game.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:06.580
So they gracefully pick up 3 flags which leaves 1 flag for team B to pick up.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.660
So there were many mistakes in the way the teams played.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:13.440
We shouldn't judge them too harshly because they didn't have too much to figure this out.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:16.660
But if you find yourself in such a situation on the game show,

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:20.180
you should always be able to figure out the optimal move.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:23.020
Did you figure out this problem?

